Use the standard AppCasting pattern: normalize the parameter name, track whether each line was handled, warn on unknown config, validate values, and call `registerVariables()` from both `OnStartUp()` and `OnConnectToServer()`.

```cpp
bool MyApp::OnStartUp()
{
  AppCastingMOOSApp::OnStartUp();

  STRING_LIST params;
  m_MissionReader.GetConfiguration(GetAppName(), params);

  for(string line : params) {
    string orig  = line;
    string param = biteStringX(line, '=');

    param = tolower(stripBlankEnds(param));
    string value = stripBlankEnds(line);

    bool handled = false;

    if(param == "threshold") {
      handled = true;

      if(!isNumber(value)) {
        reportConfigWarning("Bad threshold value: " + value);
      } else {
        m_threshold = atof(value.c_str());
      }
    }

    if(!handled)
      reportUnhandledConfigWarning(orig);
  }

  registerVariables();
  return true;
}

bool MyApp::OnConnectToServer()
{
  registerVariables();
  return true;
}

void MyApp::registerVariables()
{
  AppCastingMOOSApp::RegisterVariables();

  Register("SOME_MAIL_VAR", 0);
}
```

Key fixes:

- Unknown mission-file parameters are reported with `reportUnhandledConfigWarning(orig)`.
- Parameter names are stripped and lowercased, so `Threshold = 5` works.
- Values are validated before use.
- `registerVariables()` is called in `OnStartUp()` and `OnConnectToServer()`, which prevents missed subscriptions if startup/connect timing changes.
- `AppCastingMOOSApp::OnStartUp()` and `AppCastingMOOSApp::RegisterVariables()` are preserved.
